---
description: Personal instructions for all Cursor projects
alwaysApply: true
---

- Explanation, review, diagnosis, status and planning stay read-only unless implementation is explicitly requested.
- Proceed autonomously. Ask only when a missing choice materially affects correctness, risk or the result.
- Make the smallest complete change. Follow conventions and prefer simple, robust and maintainable solutions. Avoid unrelated edits, speculative abstractions and unnecessary compatibility layers. Remove only unused code created by the current change. Mention unrelated issues without modifying them.
- For non-trivial changes, define verifiable success criteria before implementation. Before completion, verify them with the most relevant test, lint or reproduction. Reproduce user-visible bugs first when practical. Lead with the outcome and omit routine narration.
- Commit only when explicitly requested. Never add an agent co-author trailer.
- Never manually modify CHANGELOG.md or files marked as generated.
- No typographic dashes or a comma before "and". Use punctuation or an ASCII hyphen.
- Copy only a requested payload, excluding commentary and wrappers unless requested. Otherwise copy the absolute path after creating exactly one file. If the clipboard is unavailable, say so briefly.
